        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "What is the value of $\\frac{2}{5}\\int_{1}^{2}\\frac{3}{2\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right){ln}^{2}(4\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right))}\\,\\text{d}x?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's set $u=\\log{\\left(4 x \\right)}.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\u27f9\\,1\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\operatorname{ln}\u20614$ | $\\operatorname{ln}\u20618$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}\\int_{1}^{2}\\frac{3}{2\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right){ln}^{2}(4\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right))}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{3}{5}\\int_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{(\\operatorname{ln}(4\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)))^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{3}{5}\\int_{\\operatorname{ln}4}^{\\operatorname{ln}8}\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot {(-{u}^{-1})}\\right)|_{\\operatorname{ln}4}^{\\operatorname{ln}8} \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{u})}\\right)|_{\\operatorname{ln}4}^{\\operatorname{ln}8} \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(-\\frac{3}{2}(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}8}-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}4})\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(-\\frac{3}{2}(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}{2}^{3}}-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}{2}^{2}})\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(-\\frac{3}{2}(\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}2}-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}2})\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(-\\frac{3}{2}(-\\frac{1}{6\\operatorname{ln}2})\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{4\\operatorname{ln}2}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
